      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "11 FR 14645, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "bc1904905adb4235e2982247bafd792eefc03dbd2b6addea292de9b2ab1c4021",
        "signing_date": "1946-12-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9814.txt",
        "text_sha256": "fdcf72d09780c8b2f139408fcea7142b4b35b2986fa5c6eeead6a07ea2749217",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-12-25/pdf/FR-1946-12-25.pdf"
      },
      "text": "1. There is hereby established a board \nof three members, which shall be known \n-As the President’ s Amnesty Board. The \nmembers of the Board shall be appointed \nby the President, who shall also designate \nits chairman."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2461,
      "char_start": 1490,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9814#2",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "2.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9814#2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "11 FR 14645, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "bc1904905adb4235e2982247bafd792eefc03dbd2b6addea292de9b2ab1c4021",
        "signing_date": "1946-12-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9814.txt",
        "text_sha256": "fdcf72d09780c8b2f139408fcea7142b4b35b2986fa5c6eeead6a07ea2749217",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-12-25/pdf/FR-1946-12-25.pdf"
      },
      "text": "2. The Board, under such regulations \nas it may prescribe, shall examine and \nconsider the cases of all persons con­\nvicted of violation of the Selective Train­\ning and Service Act of 1940, as amended \n(50 U. S. C. App. 301 ff.), or of any rule \nor regulation prescribed under or pur­\nsuant to that Act, or convicted of a con­\nspiracy to violate that Act or any rule or \nregulation prescribed under or pursuant \nthereto. In any case in which it deems if \ndesirable to do so, the Board shall make \na report to the Attorney General which \nshall include its findings and its recom­\nmendations as to whether Executive \nclemency should be granted or denied, \nand, in any case in which it recommends \nthat Executive clemency be granted, its \nrecommendations with respect to the \nform that such clemency should take. \nThe Attorney General shall report the \nfindings and recommendations of the \nBoard to the President, with such further \nrecommendations as he may desire to make."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2633,
      "char_start": 2462,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:9814#3",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "3.",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "scope_id": "EO:9814#3",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "11 FR 14645, PDF pages 1-1",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "bc1904905adb4235e2982247bafd792eefc03dbd2b6addea292de9b2ab1c4021",
        "signing_date": "1946-12-23",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_9814.txt",
        "text_sha256": "fdcf72d09780c8b2f139408fcea7142b4b35b2986fa5c6eeead6a07ea2749217",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1946-12-25/pdf/FR-1946-12-25.pdf"
      },
      "text": "3. The members of the Board shall\nserve without compensation, but shall be \nentitled to necessary expenses incurred \nto the performance of their duties under this order, *"
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2844,
      "char_start": 2634,
